---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const description = `${site.name} is ${site.author}'s personal magazine of commentary. No tracking, no ads.`;
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <main class="wrap page-wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h1>About<sup>The magazine</sup></h1>
    </div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>ChuckWise is the personal magazine of Chuck Houseworth. It lives at chouseworth.com. The work is commentary — essays, short takes, and reviews — mostly his. Pieces go up when they are ready.</p>
        <p>The pieces on the site right now are sample placeholders. They are here so the pages, the type, and the path from a note to a published URL can be seen before the real archive is moved over. They are not reports. They do not quote real people, and they do not cite real sources.</p>
        <p>A piece is a Markdown file, often written in Obsidian. If it is marked as a draft, it stays off the site. Publishing is a static build on Cloudflare Pages. There is no account, no analytics script, and no ad.</p>
        <h2 id="colophon">Colophon</h2>
        <p>The wordmark is Anton. Headlines and quotations are Playfair Display. Everything else is Inter. The paper is a warm off-white, the ink is near-black, and there is one red.</p>
        <p>The site is built with Astro and served as plain HTML. Fonts are stored with the site, so reading it does not call a third-party font host.</p>
        <h2 id="subscribe">Subscribe</h2>
        <p>There is no newsletter and no email list. New pieces show up in the RSS feed. Add it to a reader, or open it in the browser.</p>
        <a class="feed-url" href="/rss.xml">/rss.xml</a>
      </div>
      <aside class="about-side">
        <div class="box">
          <span class="label">The editor</span>
          <p>{site.author}</p>
          <p>{site.tagline}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box">
          <span class="label">What a post needs</span>
          <ol>
            <li>A title</li>
            <li>A type: essay, short take, or review</li>
            <li>A date</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Set draft to true and the file stays unpublished.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
